  "note": "Municipal elections, 17 May 1961: four councillors for each of the three wards. Only Town Hall Ward was contested; in Harryville and Market Wards four candidates each were declared elected without a poll. The unopposed members are taken from the returning officer's notice of result (John Simpson, returning officer, Town Clerk's Office, Town Hall, Ballymena, dated 18 May 1961; Ballymena Observer, 25 May 1961, p. 7). No party labels are printed. Returned unopposed."
